+## 3. Experimental design — Exp-1: H_C minimal assignment, pre/post measurement on naturally occurring cross-office tasks
+
+**Decision question it decides:** "Do cells (H_B) beat the minimal assignment (H_C) on the Town's actual class of cross-office work?" (One office as owner: the H_C arm names one existing office as the next-action owner.)
+
+- **Shape:** naturally occurring cross-office tasks — **not synthetic**. Sample drawn from Antonina board trails: originating issues whose threads span ≥ 2 offices; examples already cited: #315 canonical-checkout-integrity (open since 2026-10-19, "no single named owner across sponsor, red-teamer, Clerk and Examiner"); the 72-minute Executive handoff stall (`records/research/2026-10-19-office-continuity-handoff.md`); #301-related handoff/dispatch cases. Complement: `records/handoffs/`, `records/institutional-cases/index.json`, `state/handoffs/`, board trail rows with office posts.
+- **Cohorts:** Cohort A (pre-period, n_A): measured as-is; Cohort B (post-period, n_B): comparable window, each task elevated with H_C (the existing-office elevation in the originating thread). Compare: ΔID, ΔOFT, ΔRW, ΔRC, OV, LT.
+- **What is observed:** (a) Antonina board — issue threads (posts by office, timestamps, Act 18 §2 stage markers: proposal/enactment/deployment/verification/terminal; Act 18 terminal updates), act 30 §7 digest lines, worktree logs via `antonina agent log/status` (per R2's method); (b) Git — commits/branches with `Delivery-By`/`Reviewed-By`/`Integrated-By` trailers, `records/tracking/` entries with owners, `records/handoffs/` queue entries, `records/suite-status.json`, Act 21/28 artifacts (exact candidate commit + tree, verifier role); (c) Box state — liveness/reset-sequence files, resource-safety deferrals (Act 13).
+- **Predicted outcomes:**
+  - **H_C correct:** ΔID ≈ 0 (within ±15% noise), CO_B ≈ 0 (additive annotations only), RC_B = RC_A → cells unnecessary; adopt H_C default ("none" for cells: the minimal assignment predicts baseline).
+  - **H_B correct:** ΔID_B − ID_C ≥ 25% AND CO_B > 0 AND RC_B ≥ RC_A → adopt cells for this class (Exp-2 confirms).
+  - Mixed → refine thresholds; document the H_B adoption threshold from measured overhead ratio.
+- **Sample size (order of magnitude, uncertainty marked):** n = **5–10 per cohort** (cross-office tasks in a quiet town: the Town produces a handful of multi-office tasks per window; design requires ≥ 3 in each cohort). Uncertainty: time effects are day-scale; small n — treat the result as a small-n, sequential A/B ("one case tests feasibility, not a general effect" — Clerk; design for direction, not p-values); duration: 2–4 box restarts (compare across the 24 h restart boundary per Constitution VIII §1).
+- **Guard — preserving §independent review (Act 15):** every cell/elevation terminal update must carry independent verification (Act 15 §5 liveness; Act 21 §2 suite-status on the exact candidate; Act 23 §5.1 independent closure; Act 28 attestation where applicable). Measure RC = RC_C. Kill on RC drop. Every cell task overlapping another office's authority (Act 8 §2, Act 9.7 territory, Act 12) is excluded: escalate to the normal channel (parliament/legislature per Act 31 §4). Cell proceeds only on reversible actions (Act 30 §5). Cells creating new seat convening respect the Act 13 headroom floors (2 GiB; Act 13 §1); the experiment measures deferrals. Act 23 §9.2: open continuity obligations in cells remain discoverable; cells must not silently drop them. Act 30 §8: the experiment records its own reversibility (the elevation records are additive and removable).
+- **Restart durability:** cell/elevation records additive under `records/` (Act 31 §3.1 — land on green suite without review), annotated with "experiment: H_C/H_B candidate; owner: Executive Innovation Office; remove by <date>". Box restarts per Constitution VIII §1: measure "cell owner after restart = named owner" (durable records in Git/board); no re-derivation after restart.
+- **Fallback if inconclusive:** decision = **H_C default** (minimal assignment; additive, reversible; "Owner" status standing per Office 4th round); cells rejected at n = 5-10 without clear gain; adopt the Exp-2 (cell vs standing office) design when new comparable cases accumulate per the Clerk threshold; keep the Office's "separation is persuasive but evidence thin" view as the default reading.
