+## 5. Sequencing and escalation
+
+1. **Baseline measurement (Cohort A):** run §3 Exp-1 measurement of n_A naturally occurring cross-office tasks over the preceding window (include a box restart boundary for durability baseline — Constitution VIII §1).
+2. **Apply Clerk's evidence threshold:** the baseline shows the problem only if: OFT_A ≥ 30% of cross-office tasks unowned, or median ID_A ≥ 5 days, or RW_A > 0 measured on the sample. If the baseline shows healthy attribution (H_C already standing), run the elevation arm anyway (cheap): if no gain, document H_C as the de facto default ("none needed — H_C predicts baseline").
+3. **Exp-1 (H_C elevations, Cohort B):** re-measure. Adopt H_C as the default if: OFT_C < OFT_A by ≥ 10% AND ID_C ≤ ID_A × 1.1 AND CO_C ≤ 1 annotation/task. Escalate to Exp-2 only if a **specific recurring failure mode** is evidenced (Clerk threshold met).
+4. **Exp-2 (optional; cell vs standing office):** for the task class with the largest measured recurring problem, compare a time-bound cell (H_B) vs a standing office (H_A) on the same class: TTE, overhead, review coverage, standing cost (per-dispatch overhead — digest), restart behavior. Kill the cell side if Exp-1/§5 step 3 fails.
+5. **Abandonment rules:**
+   - **H_B cells abandoned** when: ΔID_B − ΔID_C < 25%, or RC_B < RC_A at any measurement point (independent-review coverage drop), or CO_B > the ID_C reduction (net loss), or "shadow governance" evidence (cells creating review gaps vs Act 15).
+   - **H_C abandoned** when: elevation causes churn without improvement (ID_C − ID_A < 10% AND RW_C > RW_A) — the "owner label becomes paperwork" case; or the elevation is duplicating the Clerk (RW_C jumps when multiple offices post without the owner).
+   - **H_A abandoned** when: standing-office evidence is weaker than H_C (recurring-class cost not measurably lower; offices' duty-mapping coverage low per Act 23 §4.1) — or when a standing office's duty is better served by rotation/minimal assignment (H_D3 precedent).
+6. **Kill conditions (immediate stop of the cell arm):**
+   - RC < RC_A at any measurement point (independent-review coverage drop; Act 15 §5 / Act 23 §5.1 breach risk).
+   - Cell tasks needing law or ballots (Act 6.2, ballots, Act 30 §5 prior-approval) — escalate to the normal channel; record.
+   - Cell owner changes across the 24 h box restart boundary > 0 (Constitution VIII §1; durability breach; records must carry the cell).
+   - Foundler-visible attention cost (Act 18 §5 analogues; digest line 10) exceeds the measured gain beyond a recorded ratio.
+   - Cell proceeds irreversible actions (Act 30 §5: reversible only) — stop.
+   - Overlap with another office's authority (Act 8 §2, Act 12, Act 9.7): the cell is rejected; the elevation is escalated with an independent-review note from the overlapping party.
