+- **Target text:** LAWS.md:188–194 (§1 archive ≥8; §2 replay harness; §3 report; §4 held-out; §5 drift; §6 maintenance; §7 falsifiers).
+- **Simplified form:** Keep §1, §3, §4, §7 (fold §5 alarm semantics into Act 33 meter + §7 text).
+- **Benefit:** Predicted overhead reduction in Act 20 instrumentation for permanent instruments (Act 20 covers trials? no — Act 20's calculus is for the trial regime in fact: Act 20 §8 says P1–P5 are carried into the ledger (LAWS.md:214); Act 20 §4 held-out for 25%+2 by Clerk — is this the same regime as Act 33 §1/§4LAWS.md:767? — measure-benefit unmeasured.)
+- **Cost:** High; regression risk: permanent instruments may lose Act 20-era quality experience.
+- **Invariant compatibility:** Act 33 unchanged; Act 22 §7 (LAWS.md:214) carried into ledger — unchanged; Act 32 §9C gate (LAWS.md:657–663) — unchanged.
+- **Minimal experiment:** Pilot: Act 33 meter under 4-core vs 7-clause rule for known-answer case set (10 cases/3 instruments, LAWS.md:188); compare telemetry overhead, TP/FP, and whether recorded readings changed (falsifier: TP<1.0, FP>0 — LAWS.md:194).
+
+### C4 — Act 18 automation of terminal-stage postings
+- **Target text:** LAWS.md:169–177 + `board-trail-check.sh:2–17`.
+- **Simplified form:** Extend `board-trail-check.sh`/`board-trail-refresh.sh` (inventory) to post, per issue with a derived terminal state and no stage marker, one concise terminal transition line (deterministic stage = the derived terminal state).
+- **Benefit:** Predicted attention saving; not measured.
