+## 4. Global high-value simplification (if the map supports it)
+
+**Proposed master gate: "The delivery-event gate."** One gate verifying a main-branch landing:
+1. Act 21/28 exact-commit suite gate — verified candidate commit + tree, suite green on it (LAWS.md:199–204; Act 28).
+2. Integrator's generated record as the durable evidence anchor (Act 31 §4; Act 28 carrier; `suite-status.sh`, `integrator.py`).
+3. Independent review only for non-additive changes (Act 31 §3, LAWS.md:480).
+4. Consumer notes: Act 26 pre-landing timing folded into the carrier-before-integration ordering (Act 28 §6.1); Act 23 §5.1 + Act 18 §2 become generated-artifact readers (board-trail-check).
+
+**Benefit claim (predicted):** reduces three paths (review + pre-landing + human-facing gaps) to one enforced path + generated artifacts; predicted to cut the attention cost of a landing by one review cycle (the cost of a landing — small per Act 8 §4; experiments: M17 = predicted 20–30% reduction).
+
+**Cost of change:** high (re-legalizes integration); **regression risk:** replacing human verification with generated evidence (real risk); **compliance:** none structurally; **Experiments:** (a) census of non-additive vs additive changes on main; (b) pilot "auto-approve when board-trail-check green + non-additive suite-green" for one week; measure revert rate (design).
+
+**Honest digestible form:** "The single master gate is the delivery-verification bundle (exact-commit suite gate + integrator artifacts); Act 26 and Act 23 §5.1 become redundant consumer notes over generated artifacts; keep the review step (Act 31 §3) as the one human gate."
